  "content": "Homage to the Three Jewels.Homage to the Great Destroyer of the Thousandfold.Then, Brahmā and Mahābrahmā,Rising, joined their palms and bowed.The Great Destroyer of the Thousandfold,This well-spoken vidyā-mantra,Which brings benefit to the childish,I shall now utter this vidyā-mantra.To the one who first in this worldRevealed the supreme vidyā-mantra,The King of Dharma, the Maker of Light,Homage to the Buddha’s splendor.To the exceptionally sublime Dharma,To the Saṅgha, the supreme assembly,And having prostrated at the feet of the Buddha,Brahmā addressed these words:Whatever Buddhas and Pratyekabuddhas,And the Śrāvakas of the Buddha,The Sages and the Guardians of the World,And however many gods there may be,All of these, within the world of humans,Have originated solely from this.Regarding the Great Sage entering the womb,There are yakṣas and rākṣasas here.Whom kings are unable to see,Nor can they even be described.Those who are not attached to a child,And those who do not dwell in a womb,When a man and woman unite,They cause the senses to become intoxicated.The oval and the oblong stages of the embryo,They ruin the seed of the child.They cause the womb to prolapse,Harm the placenta so it does not emerge;I shall now speak their names,Lord of the World, listen to me.Mañjuka and Mṛgarāja,Śuṣka, Apasmāra, and Muṣṭika,Mātṛkā and Jāmika,Kāminī and Revatī.Pūtanā and Maṭanandī,Śakuni and Kaṇṭhapāṇinī,Mukhamaṇḍitikā and Lambā,All of these roam upon the earth.These fifteen spiritsCause terror in children.I shall now describe the signs and formsOf those who seize children.When seized by Mañjuka,The eyes are caused to roll about.When seized by Mṛgarāja,Violent and unbearable vomiting occurs.When seized by Śuṣka,The eyes are caused to roll about.The Emaciator causes the child to tremble;When seized by Apasmāra,They wander and emit such sounds,And saliva and nasal mucus flow forth.When seized by Muṣṭika,They clench and unclench their fists.When seized by Mātṛkā,They laugh and likewise emit sounds.When seized by Jāmika,They clearly have no desire to nurse.When seized by Kāminī,They fall asleep in bed and cry out.When seized by Revatī,They bite their tongue with their teeth.When seized by Pūtanā,They wail and emit sounds.When seized by Mātṛnandā,Various forms manifest as physical symptoms.If seized by the Bird demon,A foul odor will arise.If seized by the Stiff-Necked demon,The throat will become completely obstructed.When seized by Mukhamanditi,They are afflicted with fever and diarrhea.When seized by Lambinī,Hiccups and gasping occur.I shall describe the formsIn which they frighten children.Ajimapā has the form of an ox,And the King of Deer resembles a deer.Skem-byed-pa has the form of a youth,Brjed-byed-pa resembles a fox,Khu-tshur-can has the form of a crow,And that Mātṛkā has the form of a goat.Jāmika has the form of a horse,'Dod-pa-can has the form of a vajra,Nam-gru has the form of a dog,And Srul-po has the form of a hand.Ma-dga'-byed-pa has the form of a cat,Śakuni has the form of a bird,Gnya'-lag-can has the form of a rooster,And Bzhin-brgyan has the form of an owl.Mig-'phyang-ba has the form of a bat.These beings terrify children;These wicked ones who snatch away childrenCause fear to the little ones.Having been drawn forth by the noose of the sūtra,They shall be thoroughly summoned.The great yakṣa general,Known as the gandharva Candana,Having bestowed that letter and seal,\"Go, and those fierce spirits,Those fifteen, summon them,\"Thus a messenger was sent.Instantly, they were all summonedWhile being bound by the five bonds.Then, to the Protector of the World,Great Brahmā, with palms joined, spoke these words:\"These who destroy the seeds of living beings,These spirits have arrived.Here in the presence of the Protector,I shall declare their punishment.\"Those women who desire a child,And those who wish to sustain their pregnancy,Should, on the eighth and fourteenth days,Take the vows and take refuge in the sublime Dharma.One should make excellent offerings to the stupa,Having bathed and become finely adorned,And having scattered white mustard seeds upon the ground,One should decorate it with flowers and incense.One should encircle the perimeterWith threads of five different colors.Having remained there until midnight,And having placed white mustard seeds upon the crown of the head,It is that which was thoroughly performed by Brahmā,And it shall be spoken as that which was emanated by Brahmā.For a period of twelve years,It shall bring benefit to the youths.Whoever transgresses against this vidyā-mantraOf the sūtra emanated by Brahmā,Like the cluster of an arjaka flower,Their head shall split into seven pieces.Tadyathā: Amge, bamge, bhange, bhavane, inanadi, binanadi, suluri, girigiri, śavari, garuni, śaruni, giri, avare locane, lasane, rocane, alabhe, angane, alabhe, talabhe, pakarṣini svāhā.May there be well-being in the womb!May the sense faculties develop perfectly!May the one dwelling in the womb be at ease!May the newborn not perish!May there be well-being in the womb!May the birth occur at the proper time!With multi-colored threads,And unbroken grains of white mustard—These are said to provide protection.May the children live long!Then, the omniscient TeacherSpoke these vidyā-mantras:May the one dwelling in the womb be protected!May the children be at ease!Tadyathā: Bodhi bodhi, mahābodhi, bodha anumate, phalini, bahuphale, śikṣa śikṣa, sāravate, sāgale, durāsade, durāgame, śūraprāpate, śūrapate, bhage, bhagā bhage, bhageni nivāraṇi svāhā.Then, the fifteen spiritsWho perpetually drink bloodBowed down to the Protector of the World,And joining their palms, they spoke these words:In any village, home, or city,Wherever this well-spokenSutra remains,The children there shall not die.Great Sage, just as you are, I shall follow accordingly. Homage to the Buddha, the Blessed One. Homage to Brahmā. May the words of the secret mantra be accomplished! May they be accomplished! May the vidyā-mantra bring liberation! May Brahmā take heed! Svāhā!The dhāraṇī that pacifies the fifteen great spirits of children is complete.",
